s. In the event that any named candidate is replaced as the nominee of their respective party prior to election day, the name in the contract will be updated and the market will resolve based on the replacement nominee of the party.\\n\\nIf the reported value falls exactly between two brackets, then this market will resolve to the higher margin bracket.\\n\\nIf two or more candidates tie for the most valid votes in this election, and the tie is between two candidates listed, this market will resolve to the lowest margin bracket for the candidate whose ballot-listed last name comes first in alphabetical order. If the tie is between a listed candidate and an unlisted candidate, this market will resolve to the lowest margin bracket for the listed candidate. If the tie is between two or more unlisted candidates, this market will resolve to \\\"Other.\\\" If the listed candidate is represented in this market group as \\\"Republican\\\" or \\\"Democrat\\\" their ballot-listed last name will still be used for tiebreaking.\\n\\nThis market will resolve based on the official vote count once the count has been made official.\\n\\nIf the election results are not known definitively by June 30, 2027, 11:59 PM ET, this market will resolve to \\\"Other\\\".\\n\\nIf a recount is initiated before the vote total has been made official, the market will remain open until the recount is completed and the vote is made official.\\n\\nThe primary resolution source for this market will be the official results of the 2026 Rhode Island Senate election as published by the state electoral authority responsible for certifying the results of the election; however, an overwhelming consensus of credible reporting may also be used.\", \"probs\": {\"150144\": {\"Yes\": 0.004, \"No\": 0.996}, \"150145\": {\"Yes\": 0.006, \"No\": 0.994}, \"150146\": {\"Yes\": 0.011, \"No\": 0.989}, \"150147\": {\"Yes\": 0.0235, \"No\": 0.9765}, \"150148\": {\"Yes\": 0.0255, \"No\": 0.9745}, \"150149\": {\"Yes\": 0.161, \"No\": 0.839}, \"150022\": {\"Yes\": 0.205, \"No\": 0.795}, \"150023\": {\"Yes\": 0.595, \"No\": 0.405}}}","lang":"en"}]],[["2729451284422881323","broadcasts"],[{"id":"cns","type":"iframe","url":"https://player.twitch.tv/?channel=afc_east_division"}]],[["2728209324273963040","broadcasts"],[{"id":"betby_trading","type":"iframe","url":"{\"rules\": \"This market will resolve to \\\"Yes\\\" if NuScale announces that it will file for bankruptcy or has filed for bankruptcy of any variety by the listed date, 11:59 PM ET. An announcement will suffice for a \\\"Yes\\\" resolution, regardless of if or when the actual filing occurs. The announcement must be made through any of their official or verified channels, as a recorded or written statement by their CEO, legal representation, or other individual or team which officially represents NuScale. A definitive consensus of credible reporting may also be used.\\n\\n\\\"NuScale\\\" refers to NuScale Power Corporation (NYSE: SMR), the parent company of the NuScale group, its operating subsidiary NuScale Power, LLC, or any other entity that is controlled by, or is under common control with, NuScale Power Corporation and that holds, directly or indirectly, all or substantially all of NuScale's business and assets at the time of the filing or announcement. Unless named above, foreign entities, financing entities, special purpose vehicles, and entities used to separate specific legal liabilities will not qualify, even if they meet that test.\\n\\nA filing for bankruptcy means a petition by an entity this market refers to (each, a \\\"covered entity\\\") under Chapter 7 or Chapter 11 of the United States Bankruptcy Code, or a bankruptcy case for a covered entity filed in a court outside the United States under that country's bankruptcy or insolvency law, including a court-appointed administration. A petition filed against a covered entity by its creditors will qualify only if the court enters an order for relief on that petition by the listed date.\\n\\nAn announcement must state that a covered entity has decided to file for bankruptcy, or has filed for bankruptcy. Statements that the company is considering, exploring, or open to bankruptcy, or that bankruptcy is one of several options, will not qualify.\\n\\nA definitive consensus of credible reporting may be used to confirm that a qualifying announcement or filing occurred. Reports citing unnamed sources that a covered entity plans or is preparing to file will not qualify on their own.\\n\\nOnce a qualifying filing or announcement occurs, this market will resolve to \\\"Yes\\\" even if the petition is later withdrawn, dismissed, or converted, or the company later reverses its decision.\\n\\nThe following will not qualify on their own: a missed payment or other default on debt; a breach of a loan covenant; foreclosure or other enforcement action by creditors; a credit rating downgrade; a debt exchange or other restructuring agreed outside of court; the appointment of a receiver; and an assignment for the benefit of creditors.\\n\\nIf a covered entity stops existing because of a merger or similar transaction, it will no longer be a covered entity. If, after the merger, no covered entity remains, this market will resolve to \\\"No\\\". If the transaction only changes a covered entity's name, state of incorporation, or legal form, or places a new holding company over the same business, the resulting entity will be treated as that covered entity.\\n\\nA filing occurs at the time recorded by the court. An announcement occurs at the time it is first published by a covered entity or its representative.\", \"probs\": {\"150144\": {\"Yes\": 0.105, \"No\": 0.895}, \"150145\": {\"Yes\": 0.195, \"No\": 0.805}, \"150146\": {\"Yes\": 0.305, \"No\": 0.695}}}","lang":"en"}]],[["2715972950330314782","broadcasts"],[{"id":"betby_trading","type":"iframe","url":"{\"rules\": \"This is a market on predicting the date when the UK general election will be officially c